o</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Purification, cloning, and expression of an apyrase from the bed bug <italic>Cimex lectularius</italic>. A new type of nucleotide-binding enzyme</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><year>1998</year><volume>273</volume><fpage>30583</fpage><lpage>30590</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9804829</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1074/jbc.273.46.30583</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Valenzuela</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><name><surname>Belkaid</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Rowton</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ribeiro</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The salivary apyrase of the blood-sucking sand fly <italic>Phlebotomus papatasi </italic>belongs to the novel <italic>Cimex </italic>family of apyrases</article-title><source>J Exp Biol</source><year>2001</year><volume>204</volume><fpage>229</fpage><lpage>237</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11136609</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cheeseman</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Characterization of apyrase activity from the salivary glands of the cat flea <italic>Ctenocephalides felis</italic></article-title><source>Insect Biochem Mol Biol</source><year>1998</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>1025</fpage><lpage>1030</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9887518</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0965-1748(98)00093-9</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ribeiro</surname><given-names>JMC</given-names></name><name><surname>Vaughan</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Azad</surname><given